> 
> I guess the difficult bit is {jai bu'u}. {jai bu'u} is similar to a cmavo from
> selma'o SE. It re-orders the arguments of a brivla, bringing in this case
> the bu'u-argument to x1 and sending the old x1 to a new place tagged
> with {fai}.
> 
> So for example, if you have:
> 
>     mi tavla do bu'u lo panka
>     I talk to you in the park.
> 
> you can transform it, by re-ordering the places of {tavla}, into:
> 
>     lo panka cu jai bu'u tavla do fai mi
>     The park is where talk to you I.
So 'the place in which I am happy is Toronto' would be 
{lo jai bu'u gleki be fai mi cu me la torontos}? 
